# Build context for every image built from the repository root: Dockerfile and
# Dockerfile.alpine, whose `COPY . .` takes everything not excluded here, and
# test/Dockerfile.run, which the test/compose*.yml suites build with
# `context: ..` and which copies the binaries out of bin/.
#
# Only paths git does not track belong in this file, and .git must stay out of
# it. The builder runs `go build` in a git checkout, so the toolchain stamps
# vcs.revision, vcs.time and vcs.modified into both binaries, and --version
# prints them (internal/version.Full). Without .git that stamp is gone. And
# vcs.modified is `git status`: a tracked file excluded here reads as deleted
# in the builder and marks every binary "dirty".
#
# What this list is for is keeping untracked local material -- secrets, agent
# worktrees, build output -- out of the context and the builder's layers. It
# is not what keeps the stamp clean: the builder's `git status` honours
# .gitignore, which is in the context, and everything excluded here is ignored
# there too. An untracked file named in neither still marks the build dirty.
#
# Unlike .gitignore, a pattern here is anchored at the context root, so the
# ones that should match at any depth say **/.

# Local secrets and environment files.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Agent session data, including git worktrees: a build from the main checkout
# would otherwise send every worktree under .claude/worktrees with it.
.claude/

# Build and test output, mirroring .gitignore -- except bin/, which stays in:
# test/Dockerfile.run copies bin/openvox-ca and bin/openvox-ca-ctl from it.
dist/
/openvox-ca
/openvox-ca-ctl
**/*.exe
**/*.test
**/*.out
coverage.html
.test-output/
tmp/
.mage/
**/node_modules/

# Editor and OS clutter, mirroring .gitignore.
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
**/*.swp
**/*.swo

# Untracked local material, mirroring .gitignore.
docs/superpowers/
Threat_Model/
